      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:definition": {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "This term may have subtle variations in its definition depending on the type of organism it relates to. In a general sense, it applies to organisms that are at the last stage of their juvenile development prior to a fully mature adult stage, ie when an organism looks like an adult but its reproductive organs have not yet reached maturity."
      },
